# End-to-end EMULATOR test for the UltiMachine Archim2 (Atmel SAM3X8E)
# in DETERMINISTIC TICK MODE. Boots klipper firmware under Renode
# against the archim2 pin map, completes klippy identify + clocksync,
# brings up the full MCU config (4 TMC2130s on software SPI, 2
# software-PWM heaters, a fan, endstops, 2 thermistors), reads the
# thermistors through the SAM3X ADC, round-trips the TMC2130 register
# files over the software SPI chain, and exercises interactive gcode
# (M114/M105) against real firmware.
#
# This is the SAM3X per-printer test, the counterpart to sam3x_smoke
# (boot only). It reuses two existing pieces of infrastructure intact:
#
#   - The TMC SPI chain responder (renode_hooks spi_tmc). The four
#     TMC2130s use SOFTWARE SPI, but software SPI still routes every
#     datagram through the firmware's spidev_transfer (src/spicmds.c) -
#     the single hw+sw SPI chokepoint - so the same PC-skip responder
#     duet3-6hc (TMC5160) and octopus-pro (TMC5160 sw SPI) use serves
#     these reads with no change. DUMP_TMC below reads the live register
#     file for stepper_x and the extruder; the IOIN read returning
#     version=0x30 is the positive proof the SPI read path round-tripped.
#
#   - The SAM4S ADC stub (test/emulator/sam4s_adc_stub.py). src/atsam/
#     adc.c is shared between SAM3X and SAM4S and the ADC register map is
#     identical, so the same stub serves the SAM3X ADC verbatim at the
#     SAM3X base 0x400C0000. The hotend reads through ADC channel index
#     12 (PB19, ATC Semitec 104GT-2) and the bed through index 13 (PB20,
#     EPCOS 100K). With a broken ADC both heaters sit at temp=0.0 with no
#     shutdown, so the "temp=3" assertion below (both read ~36 C) is the
#     positive proof the ADC delivered samples.
#
# The real Archim2 host link is USB; the firmware here is the generic
# serial-mode sam3x8e build (host link on PA8/PA9) and the test
# exercises the pin map, which is independent of the host link. The
# gated path is motion-free.
DICTIONARY sam3x8e.dict
CONFIG archim2.cfg
EMULATOR archim2.fixture.json
REQUIRES_EMULATOR  # deterministic-time lockstep needs the real backend

# Interactive gcode round-trip against real firmware in tick mode.
M114
M105
# Read back the live TMC register file over the software SPI chain for
# the first and last drivers. DUMP_TMC reads every register (incl.
# IOIN) live, so it only produces a full dump if the firmware
# round-tripped the read datagrams through spidev_transfer.
DUMP_TMC STEPPER=stepper_x
DUMP_TMC STEPPER=extruder

# klippy connected, loaded the dictionary, and built the full config
# against real firmware.
EXPECT_LOG_CONTAINS "Loaded MCU 'mcu'"
EXPECT_LOG_CONTAINS "Configured MCU 'mcu'"
# DUMP_TMC dumped the first and last drivers; the IOIN read returning
# the responder's version byte (0x30) proves the software SPI chain read
# path round-tripped.
EXPECT_LOG_CONTAINS "DUMP_TMC stepper_x"
EXPECT_LOG_CONTAINS "DUMP_TMC extruder"
EXPECT_LOG_CONTAINS "version=0x30"
# Positive proof the SAM3X ADC delivered samples: both thermistors read
# ~36 C, so a periodic Stats line carries "temp=3x". A broken ADC leaves
# them at temp=0.0 with no shutdown, which this catches where the
# no-error assertions below cannot.
EXPECT_LOG_CONTAINS "temp=3"
# A broken SPI round-trip surfaces as a TMC init failure or a direct
# read error; the deterministic tick clock must produce neither.
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "failed to init"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "Unable to read tmc spi"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "Internal error"
# A renode-side crash (wrong sysbus peripheral, hook callback error)
# kills serial; klippy then gets EOF and identify / TMC init time out.
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "Got EOF when reading from device"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "failed to init: Timeout"
# With the deterministic clock the config / TMC / ADC path pushes no
# deadline into the firmware's past, so nothing shuts down.
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "ADC out of range"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "Timer too close"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "Rescheduled timer in the past"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "Klippy is shutdown"
